    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕnĕrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		genero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a begetting</i>, <i>generating</i>,
				<i>generation</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 50, 74, § 157</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">8, 47, 72,
				§ 187</span></i>: deorum = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεογονία</span>, a poem of Hesiod, <i><span class="en">Lact.
				1, 5, 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gen. 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Christi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Matt. 1, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a</i>
			
			
			<i>generation</i> of men,
				<i><span class="en">Ambros. Off. Ministr. 1, 25,
			121</span></i>.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Plin.
				20, 13, 51, § 142 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eph. 3,
				5</span></i> et saep.</div>
